        <a class="related-card" href="/tutorials/how-to-replace-a-car-battery/"><strong>How to Replace a Car Battery</strong><span>See the careful basics of a conventional 12V battery replacement.</span></a>
        <a class="related-card" href="/tutorials/how-to-change-spark-plugs/"><strong>How to Change Spark Plugs</strong><span>Follow a vehicle-specific maintenance workflow.</span></a>
        <a class="related-card" href="/tutorials/how-to-use-a-cordless-drill/"><strong>How to Use a Cordless Drill</strong><span>Build confidence with another everyday workshop tool.</span></a>
      </div></section>
      <div class="closing"><h2>Final thoughts</h2><p>A multimeter is easier to use when you match the mode, the circuit state and the probe connections to the question. Start with low voltage, keep resistance and continuity tests unpowered, and take a moment to confirm the lead jacks. A calm setup makes the reading far more useful.</p></div>
